\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces PRISMA 2020 flow of the logged search, run in October 2026 over a publication window that ends at the September 2026 cut-off (queries, dates, and counts in \ref  {app:model}); the census itself was compiled iteratively during the review, and the flow shows how the two relate. The logged queries retrieve 76\% of the census designs; most of the remainder are circuits papers that describe themselves outside the query vocabulary (a ``processor'' rather than an ``accelerator'', a milliwatt figure rather than ``edge''), which venue sweeps recover. The hand assessment found 54{} further eligible designs, none of which targets RoPE; adding them changes no conclusion of the census (\cref  {tab:robust}).}}{6}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:prisma}{{2}{6}{PRISMA 2020 flow of the logged search, run in October 2026 over a publication window that ends at the September 2026 cut-off (queries, dates, and counts in \ref {app:model}); the census itself was compiled iteratively during the review, and the flow shows how the two relate. The logged queries retrieve \precallCensus \% of the census designs; most of the remainder are circuits papers that describe themselves outside the query vocabulary (a ``processor'' rather than an ``accelerator'', a milliwatt figure rather than ``edge''), which venue sweeps recover. The hand assessment found \paudit {} further eligible designs, none of which targets RoPE; adding them changes no conclusion of the census (\cref {tab:robust})}{figure.2}{}}
