\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The edge-regime, component-aware taxonomy with representative designs. A design is placed by reading the axes in order: resource regime, inference phase, operation type and component, and finally platform, which appears only at the leaves so that one component can be compared across FPGA, ASIC, NPU, and CIM/PIM realizations. The RoPE leaf (highlighted) is consolidated in \cref  {sec:rope}; the full classification of every census design is given in \cref  {tab:census}.}}{11}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:taxonomy}{{6}{11}{The edge-regime, component-aware taxonomy with representative designs. A design is placed by reading the axes in order: resource regime, inference phase, operation type and component, and finally platform, which appears only at the leaves so that one component can be compared across FPGA, ASIC, NPU, and CIM/PIM realizations. The RoPE leaf (highlighted) is consolidated in \cref {sec:rope}; the full classification of every census design is given in \cref {tab:census}}{figure.6}{}}
\newlabel{fig:taxonomy@cref}{{[figure][6][]6}{[1][10][]11}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Robustness of the census conclusions. Each row recomputes the gap matrix (\cref  {fig:gapheat}) on a subset or a reclassification of the census; the middle columns give the cells the text relies on (several-W/single-W/mW), and the last five columns state whether each conclusion still holds. K1: GEMM is the most-targeted component overall; K2: fewer than one in ten single-watt and milliwatt designs (pooled) target RoPE; K3: at most one milliwatt design targets MoE routing; K4: at least five milliwatt designs handle the KV cache; K5: Softmax is the most-covered non-GEMM operator at milliwatt scale. The last row gives the fraction of 10000 random reclassifications (each design moved to a neighbouring power class with probability 0.2 and each component tag dropped with probability 0.1) in which the conclusion holds.}}{11}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:robust}{{3}{11}{Robustness of the census conclusions. Each row recomputes the gap matrix (\cref {fig:gapheat}) on a subset or a reclassification of the census; the middle columns give the cells the text relies on (several-W/single-W/mW), and the last five columns state whether each conclusion still holds. K1: GEMM is the most-targeted component overall; K2: fewer than one in ten single-watt and milliwatt designs (pooled) target RoPE; K3: at most one milliwatt design targets MoE routing; K4: at least five milliwatt designs handle the KV cache; K5: Softmax is the most-covered non-GEMM operator at milliwatt scale. The last row gives the fraction of 10000 random reclassifications (each design moved to a neighbouring power class with probability 0.2 and each component tag dropped with probability 0.1) in which the conclusion holds}{table.3}{}}
\newlabel{tab:robust@cref}{{[table][3][]3}{[1][10][]11}}
