\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces The RoPE hardware design space, spanned by how the rotation angle is obtained (rows) and where the rotation executes (columns). Known designs cluster in the datapath and shared-unit columns; commercial NPU stacks fall back to the CPU; and the KV-read-path column---made relevant by pre-RoPE key quantization, compressed key storage, and KV reuse (\cref  {sec:rope})---has no design with a disclosed angle-generation strategy. The first RoPE datapath in measured silicon combines a step-angle lookup with an angle-accumulation recurrence\nobreakspace  {}\cite  {liu2026subspace}. No design reconfigures its strategy between prefill and decode.}}{20}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rope}{{10}{20}{The RoPE hardware design space, spanned by how the rotation angle is obtained (rows) and where the rotation executes (columns). Known designs cluster in the datapath and shared-unit columns; commercial NPU stacks fall back to the CPU; and the KV-read-path column---made relevant by pre-RoPE key quantization, compressed key storage, and KV reuse (\cref {sec:rope})---has no design with a disclosed angle-generation strategy. The first RoPE datapath in measured silicon combines a step-angle lookup with an angle-accumulation recurrence~\cite {liu2026subspace}. No design reconfigures its strategy between prefill and decode}{figure.10}{}}
\newlabel{fig:rope@cref}{{[figure][10][]10}{[1][19][]20}}
