\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Priority map of the identified gaps. Horizontal position: implementation difficulty and risk; vertical position: latency--energy headroom a dedicated design could plausibly recover (High $>$20\%, Medium 5--20\%, Low $<$5\%); marker size: importance of the component (\cref  {tab:complexity}); colour: verdict. The map is a reasoned judgement with explicit axes, so a reader who weighs them differently can re-derive a different ordering from the same evidence.}}{29}{figure.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:priority}{{15}{29}{Priority map of the identified gaps. Horizontal position: implementation difficulty and risk; vertical position: latency--energy headroom a dedicated design could plausibly recover (High $>$20\%, Medium 5--20\%, Low $<$5\%); marker size: importance of the component (\cref {tab:complexity}); colour: verdict. The map is a reasoned judgement with explicit axes, so a reader who weighs them differently can re-derive a different ordering from the same evidence}{figure.15}{}}
