\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {C.11}{The edge-regime design census (cut-off September 2026; $n=84$). Regime classes are defined in \cref  {sec:scope}; operator-level units (phase op.) are classified by the regime of their intended integration target. Phase: P = prefill, D = decode. Components: Att = attention products, KV\$ = KV-cache handling, SM = Softmax, Norm = normalization, Act = activation. Impl.: Si = measured silicon; SoC = measured on commercial mobile silicon; FPGA = FPGA prototype; PL = post-layout; Syn = post-synthesis; Sim = simulation; NR = not stated. Rows were checked against the primary source, in full text wherever it was accessible. $^{a}$Regime inferred: power not stated in the text (only in figures) or derived from reported throughput and efficiency; $^{b}$evaluated on encoder or short-sequence Transformer workloads; $^{p}$preprint (arXiv only at the cut-off). The classification rule is given in \cref  {sec:census_rule}.}}{33}{table.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:census}{{C.11}{33}{The edge-regime design census (cut-off September 2026; $n=84$). Regime classes are defined in \cref {sec:scope}; operator-level units (phase op.) are classified by the regime of their intended integration target. Phase: P = prefill, D = decode. Components: Att = attention products, KV\$ = KV-cache handling, SM = Softmax, Norm = normalization, Act = activation. Impl.: Si = measured silicon; SoC = measured on commercial mobile silicon; FPGA = FPGA prototype; PL = post-layout; Syn = post-synthesis; Sim = simulation; NR = not stated. Rows were checked against the primary source, in full text wherever it was accessible. $^{a}$Regime inferred: power not stated in the text (only in figures) or derived from reported throughput and efficiency; $^{b}$evaluated on encoder or short-sequence Transformer workloads; $^{p}$preprint (arXiv only at the cut-off). The classification rule is given in \cref {sec:census_rule}}{table.11}{}}
\newlabel{tab:census@cref}{{[table][11][2147483647]C.11}{[1][33][]33}}
